id: pm-github-cited-issue-adoption
title: Adopt an existing item that cites the imported GitHub issue
description: "Prevent gated imports from duplicating existing prose-citing work. Add exact citation adoption after established identity matching, refuse ambiguous citations, expose receipts and an opt-out, and validate dry runs against public trackers."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog-unreleased,github,import
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:16:54.041Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T10:18:04.984Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Preserve established tag/URL/provider identity matching. Adopt only an untagged item with exactly one distinct repository-qualified GitHub issue across title, description and body, plus explicit fix/close/resolve intent, Issue:/Tracks:/GH issue labeling, or the reference in its title. Incidental and multi-issue citations never transfer ownership; return citation_candidates IDs and reasons while importing normally. Keep ambiguity refusal for two eligible intent-bearing items. Closed incidental items must not reopen. Test qualified references and punctuation, positive fix/label/title cases, related-only mentions and multi-issue roadmaps, non-git trackers, typed receipts, idempotency and opt-out. Record behavioral revert proofs. Repeat public dry runs including pre-tag pm-review adoption and pm-context counts. Local targeted tests/typecheck/lint and exact-head npm/Bun CI release gates pass."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T07:17:26.861Z",codex-agent,"Overlap review: pm-github-c093 owns structured URL/provider back-link import matching, pm-github-identity-collisions diagnoses and repairs structured ownership, Projects import matches board and issue provenance, and export upserts linked issues. None adopts arbitrary exact prose citations. This feature adds a fallback only after existing import matching, preserving those paths. Scheduled gated sync already invokes import, so it inherits the default. Plan ambiguous citations before writes and refuse the batch with actionable candidate IDs."
  "2026-10-23T07:24:01.857Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: strong ownership matching stays first; exact qualified title/description/body citations fall back to a single existing item. All imports now prepare identities before writes, and ambiguous citations expose candidate IDs plus an exact tagging remedy. Adoption retains local tags and reports a separate count; provider-owned records retain link-only behavior. New tests use real trackers with a PATH containing node and the pinned pm CLI but no git, plus real git trackers for write-gate acceptance."
  "2026-10-23T07:27:45.693Z",codex-agent,"New citation suite: 13/13 passed, including plain/atomic adoption in non-git trackers, write-gate acceptance, retry identity, ambiguity refusal, punctuation, repo/number boundaries, structured ownership precedence and provider link-only preservation. Live pm-review main aa16d855df1f7b74afd3453617f77e92c44d493e already tags pm-review-withdrawn-lineage for issue 30, so an untouched current-main copy correctly plans update rather than adopt. Preserve this current-state result and locate the pre-tag historical tracker for a separate adoption replay. SDK reads may create runtime caches; verify original tracked file bytes independently."
  "2026-10-23T07:36:10.754Z",codex-agent,"Public dry-run evidence: current pm-review main aa16d855df1f7b74afd3453617f77e92c44d493e issue 30 plans 0 creates, 1 update, 0 adopts because PR 33 already added provenance. Actual pre-tag snapshot f72250e4c5ee8dfafaf57ee8afe20ddd3cbc993e plans 0 creates, 0 updates, 1 adopt into pm-review-withdrawn-lineage; gate new_entries=0. Current pm-context main 8d9576778a3609f156e9444ed659ca7c2e2aa9e7 plans 5 issues: 2 creates, 3 updates, 0 adopts, 0 skips, not truncated. All three are plain-directory archive copies. SHA-256 comparisons verify 106/106, 106/106 and 181/181 original files unchanged. Detailed receipts are in docs/cited-issue-adoption-validation.md."
  "2026-10-23T07:38:52.136Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: an isolated scratch package retained the new planner, receipts and tests, but restored only matchImportedIssue from base main. node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts exited 1 with the expected adoption and ambiguity assertion failures. Tests import live TypeScript, so no stale build could hide the revert. The fixed worktree was never reverted and its 14 adoption regressions pass. Full npm/Bun release evidence will come from the PR CI release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T07:40:47.558Z",codex-agent,"Local checks passed: npm run typecheck; npm run build; npm run build:test; npm run lint; npm run docstring (17 files, 187 documented declarations); npm run duplication (18 authored modules, zero duplicated lines); changelog generation/check and strict tracker health. Behavioral revert: 14 tests, 10 fail and 4 pass with only the old matcher restored; fixed matcher: 14 pass, zero skips. Broader import regressions and the mandatory linked-test run are in progress. The current dependency pin is unchanged; registry CLI version was verified as 2026.10.23."
  "2026-10-23T07:42:06.837Z",codex-agent,"Mandatory linked verification completed: pm test pm-github-cited-issue-adoption --run --progress passed its one linked command, node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts (14 tests pass, zero failures/skips). Public tracker dry runs and behavioral revert evidence are complete. The ready-for-review PR will use CI npm run release:check and bun run release:check, unchanged thresholds, as full release-gate evidence; the final report will link the exact-head run and its counts. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-23T07:46:57.681Z",codex-agent,"Broader local regressions found a legacy plain-import assertion that expected an earlier issue to be written before a later structured ownership conflict. Universal identity preplanning intentionally removes that partial-write boundary. Updated the regression to require the unchanged tracker in plain, gated and atomic modes; structured matching and precedence remain unchanged. No production-code change was required. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/169."
  "2026-10-23T07:49:35.957Z",codex-agent,"Focused write-boundary regression passed: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"ambiguous later issue\" test/import-fidelity.test.ts — 3 tests pass, zero failures/skips (plain, gated, atomic). This updates the old partial-write expectation to the fail-closed preflight contract. The initial CI run still tests the prior assertion; the next pushed head will contain this test-only correction and tracker receipt."
  "2026-10-23T08:27:20.623Z",codex-agent,"Final exact-citation audit reproduced an additional boundary miss: Issue: followed immediately by the issue URL, Reference:owner/repo#N, and a sentence-ending question mark returned new instead of citation. These are qualified prose citations under the acceptance criteria. Adjusted only the regex punctuation boundaries; retained negative URL query/path and longer-number cases. Added the forms to the existing pure matching regression, so test counts stay unchanged. The final source head will receive a fresh full npm/Bun CI run."
  "2026-10-23T08:29:20.672Z",codex-agent,"Punctuation boundary verification: typecheck, test typecheck and targeted lint passed. Four pure matching checks passed with the fix. Isolated behavioral revert restored only citesIssue to the preceding implementation: 1 of 4 checks failed (3 passed), proving the expanded boundary cases detect this correction. The general adoption revert remains 10 failures / 4 passes when only matchImportedIssue is restored to base main. All mutations remain covered by the real-tracker suite and the fresh full CI run."
  "2026-10-23T08:50:08.005Z",codex-agent,"CI identified one remaining legacy matcher parity assertion: GitHub issue: immediately followed by a URL was expected to remain new. The declared-ownership parser remains unchanged, but the new exact-citation fallback correctly adopts that form. Scoped both parity-table invocations to explicit adoption opt-out, preserving the original ownership grammar contract; default colon-citation behavior remains asserted in the new adoption suite. This is a test-only correction. The failed job passed 1034/1035 tests and reported four 100 percent coverage dimensions over all 18 authored modules."
  "2026-10-23T08:51:27.741Z",codex-agent,"Focused verification passed after the parity correction: node --test test/import-regex.test.ts test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts — 21/21 pass, zero failures/skips. The full regex file was rerun with an explicit default-citation assertion for GitHub issue:URL (citation, linkOnly=false): 7/7 pass. Test typecheck and targeted lint passed. Reviewed every matchImportedIssue test call; strong ownership tests now explicitly opt out only where they assert the legacy grammar. Production source remains unchanged from bbe5718."
  "2026-10-23T09:59:05.116Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up on PR 169: broad citation matching could overwrite or reopen a related-only closed item, and selecting only one issue could adopt a multi-issue roadmap. Tighten the fallback to one distinct qualified issue across all prose fields and explicit fix/track intent or a title reference. Preserve established ownership matching, report rejected incidental candidates with IDs/reasons, and retain ambiguity refusal only for two eligible owners. Remote PR head was pulled first; merged the one newer main commit containing CodeQL action updates."
  "2026-10-23T10:14:59.028Z",codex-agent,"Review regressions: node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts test/import-regex.test.ts passed 28/28 with zero failures/skips. Both plain and atomic closed-related items remain byte-equivalent in SDK fields while an open GitHub issue imports separately; roadmaps are never adopted when either issue is selected alone or both are selected. Positive closing words/labels/title cases and ambiguity among eligible owners remain covered. Behavioral revert in an isolated source copy restored only citesIssue and matchImportedIssue from pre-review head 4220a37, leaving planner/receipt code and SDK persistence real: the closed-incidental pattern failed 2/2, and the roadmap-only pattern failed 2/2, both exit 1 with no skips. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstrings passed; the additional sorted multi-candidate receipt assertion passed its targeted check."
  "2026-10-23T10:18:02.884Z",codex-agent,"Real-data revalidation after the ownership guards: actual pre-tag pm-review f72250e4c5ee8dfafaf57ee8afe20ddd3cbc993e still plans one adopt into pm-review-withdrawn-lineage, zero creates (Fix URL description plus Issue: URL body, one distinct issue). Fresh pm-review main e1fc83a81507ca6a91f1675b74863c050f1a89f1 plans one provenance update. Fresh public pm-context main 7d7479ae77c13d01c54b2b4560ad54091ffed788 plans five issues: two creates, three updates, zero adopts/skips. Original file hashes remain unchanged 106/106, 106/106 and 181/181. The mandatory linked adoption test run passed 21/21. Strict tracker health passed after merging main; no merge maintenance was needed. Updated README examples and the validation document describe eligibility, incidental receipts and both review revert proofs."
